\subsection{Sentiment Alignment: VADER vs. RoBERTa}
Sentiment analysis forms the foundation to understanding perception shift. Utilizing a dual-model architecture over a single model for sentiment scoring ensures lexical as well as contextual awareness. VADER is a sentiment analysis tool which specializes in social media text and is capable of handling capitalization and modifiers, but fails to grasp the contextual sentiment of a word that includes sarcasm. RoBERTa is a transformed based model that understands the nuances and helps identify the sentiment correctly.

To justify the hybrid model, a subset of the TweetEval dataset($n=374$)\cite{15,16,17} is chosen and Cohen’s Kappa\cite{18} is applied to assess model alignment:

\begin{equation}
\kappa = \frac{p_o - p_e}{1 - p_e}
\label{eq:kappa}
\end{equation}

Where $p_o$ is the relative observed agreement and $p_e$ is the hypothetical probability of chance agreement.

According to the standard scale proposed by Landis and Koch\cite{19}, $\kappa = 0.146$ represents only a "Slight Agreement".

